        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0874" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg786"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Count Cassini.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The admiral at San Francisco advises me this morning that the captain of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lena</hi> writes him that the ship being unseaworthy
                    must disarm, and asks to be allowed to make needed repairs. When the President
                    shall have approved the conditions necessary to insure the neutralization of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Lena</hi> and her officers and crew until the end of
                    the war, and to permit necessary repairs, the admiral will be instructed to
                    cause the disarmament to be effected, whereupon I shall have pleasure in
                    advising you further.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
